@anon.a2b023d1a4e2834952d16152dce23780.662 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [689 x i8] }> <{ [689 x i8] c"If this is `{false}`, the items are spaced apart with\0A[term list spacing]($terms.spacing). If it is `{true}`, they use normal\0A[leading]($par.leading) instead. This makes the term list more compact,\0Awhich can look better if the items are short.\0A\0AIn markup mode, the value of this parameter is determined based on\0Awhether items are separated with a blank line. If items directly follow\0Aeach other, this is set to `{true}`; if items are separated by a blank\0Aline, this is set to `{false}`.\0A\0A```example\0A/ Fact: If a term list has a lot\0A  of text, and maybe other inline\0A  content, it should not be tight\0A  anymore.\0A\0A/ Tip: To make it wide, simply\0A  insert a blank line between the\0A  items.\0A```" }>, align 1
